@node dokgen_commands
@section (dokgen commands)

@c %start of fragment

This module defines procedures that are associated to every command
provided by the command-line interface of the @command{dokgen}
program.  See the @ref{CLI} and @xref{dokgen_cli,(dokgen cli)}
sections for additional information.


@c %end of fragment

@c %start of fragment

@subsection Procedures

@c %start of fragment

@deffn Procedure api sources OPT: destination
Extract the API documentation of the given set of Guile Scheme modules.

@strong{sources} (list of strings): Absolute or relative paths to Guile
Scheme modules that compose the code whose API documentation will be
extracted.  These paths can lead to both Scheme files or Scheme
directories.  For example:

@example 
(list «myproject/liby.scm»
      «myproject/liby»
      «myproject/libz.scm»
      «myproject/libz»)
@end example

@strong{destination} (string): Optional path to a directory where the
final Texinfo files will be saved.  If not provided,
@var{DEFAULT_DOC_PATH} is used (see the module
@ref{dokgen_commands}).

@strong{Result}: The API documentation is saved to the @var{destination}
directory.

@end deffn


@c %end of fragment

@c %end of fragment

@c %start of fragment

@subsection Variables

@c %start of fragment

@defvr Variable DEFAULT_DOC_PATH
@verbatim 
"doc/api"
@end verbatim

@end defvr


@c %end of fragment

